### bat — syntax-highlighting pager and `cat` replacement.
#
# Format: one command-line argument per line, `#` starts a comment. Every
# option here is only a default — the same flag passed on the command line
# still wins, so `bat --style=plain` keeps working.
#
# bat picks the syntax from the *file name*. Input read from a pipe has no
# name (the header shows `STDIN`) and is rendered as plain text, so colourise
# piped Markdown with `bat -l md` or `bat --file-name=answer.md`.

# A named theme paints with a fixed palette, which gives richer colours than
# the terminal's own sixteen at the cost of pinning the output to a dark
# background: on a light terminal it keeps its dark syntax colours. `ansi` is
# the theme-agnostic alternative, and the one the Git module still uses in
# color.conf and delta.conf; `bat --list-themes` shows the rest.
--theme="Catppuccin Mocha"

# Line numbers, a filename header and the surrounding grid, plus `changes` so
# the Git gutter marks added and modified lines while a tracked file is read.
--style="numbers,changes,header-filename,grid"

--tabs=4

# Colourised input (`git log --color=always | bat`) would otherwise show its
# escape sequences literally; `auto` strips them before highlighting.
--strip-ansi=auto

### Syntax mappings for file names bat does not recognise on its own.

# The Git module splits its configuration into `*.conf` includes; only the
# main `~/.config/git/config` is mapped to the Git Config syntax by default.
--map-syntax="**/.config/git/*.conf:Git Config"
--map-syntax="**/modules/git/config/.config/git/*.conf:Git Config"

# Module manifests are shell assignments sourced by the installer.
--map-syntax="module.conf:Bourne Again Shell (bash)"

# Package manifests are comment-annotated one-name-per-line lists, which is
# exactly what the pip requirements syntax highlights.
--map-syntax="packages.apt:Requirements.txt"
--map-syntax="packages.brew:Requirements.txt"

# just recipes are Makefile-shaped.
--map-syntax="justfile:Makefile"
--map-syntax=".justfile:Makefile"
--map-syntax="*.just:Makefile"
